  "description": {
    "en": "Original stylized-inspired static water-fern art, using Dorfiella knowltonii following Hermsen (2025); Hydropteris pinnata is the historical 1994 name. Round junction structures are an artistic interpretation of uncertain, possibly sporocarp-like appendages, not confirmed reproductive organs. Colors, pose and nominal dimensions are artistic.",
